        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0568" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg468"/>

                <head>No. 300.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 4, 1879</date>.
                        (Received November 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instruction No. 380, of the 15th ultimo, and in obedience thereto I
                    herewith inclose three copies of Her Majesty’s order in council, of the 14th of
                    August last, relating to the prevention of collisions at sea, which I received
                    from Lord Salisbury this morning.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d300-a1.xml" xpointer="d300-a1"/>
